theme_override_font_sizes/normal_font_size = 32
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "In Brazil, there is a game called Truco. It is a betting game, where you and a partner face two other people, counting cards, betting points and trying to make it to 12 points, before the other pair makes it. In order to do this, you will play Hands, a set of three rounds where in each round, every player will play one card of the three they have. Whoever has the highest card, wins the round. Whoever wins two rounds, wins the Hand.

Truco has a special card order, shown in the side, from left to right then top to bottom.

You can also bet your points: by calling Truco, you can raise the stakes of that hand from 1 pt to 3 pts. Of course, the other pair may refuse your bet, giving you one point and going to the next hand. But if they accept, they may still raise the stakes even higher!

Finally, you can exchange your dealt cards if you recieve only face cards. However, the cards you discard go face down into the table, so you may want to exchange even if not all of them are face cards. If you get caught, though, the other pair gets a point."
fit_content = true

